{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "All's Well That Ends Well", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Next Time", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Perfect Modals - Review", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use Perfect modals to talk about what was advisable in the past. The form of Perfect modals is: modal + have + past participle.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The following is a list of the Perfect modals and their meanings: </br> p.p.= Past participle of the verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Could have + p.p.</span> - This structure is used to talk about something that you had the chance to do, but you didn't do. Also, to speculate about the past.</br><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">could have been</span>  a better student in French class.</span></br><span class=\"italic\"> My stomach is upset - it <span class=\"strong\">could have been</span> the sushi.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Should have + p.p.</span> - This structure is used to to talk about regrets. </br> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">shouldn't have eaten</span> that sushi - now I feel sick!", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Must have + p.p.</span> - We use this structure to talk about something that you are almost certain happened.</br><span class=\"italic\">  You <span class=\"strong\">must have gone</span> to bed late last night - you look tired!", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Might/May have + p.p.</span> - We use this structure to talk about something that was possible, but you are not sure.</br><span class=\"italic\">The sushi <span class=\"strong\">might have been</span> the reason you got sick.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Would have + p.p.</span> - We use this structure to talk about an action that did not happen. </br><span class=\"italic\">If it had been sunny, we <span class=\"strong\">would have gone</span> to the beach.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">must not have gotten</span> much sleep last night - you look tired.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">shouldn't have waited</span> as long as I did to ask you out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I had asked you out earlier, <span class=\"strong\">would you have said</span> yes?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">might have done</span> that.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He <span class=\"strong\">could have helped</span> me with my homework, he <span class=\"strong\">could've played</span> games with me.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressing Willingness and Intention", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You usually use <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">will</span> </span>and <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">won't</span></span> to talk about the future. However, they do have another function - to express a willingness or an unwillingness to do something. </br>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In the present:  <span class=\"strong\">will</span> and  <span class=\"strong\">won't</span> </br></br> You can use <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">will</span></span> to say that someone is willing to do something. In other words, they are ready to do something. </br>For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">My neighbor is great - she <span class=\"strong\">will</span> always watch over my house when I'm away.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">won't</span> to express unwillingness to do something.  </br>For example: </br><span class=\"italic\"> I <span class=\"strong\">won't</span> help you study - you have to do it yourself.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In the past: <span class=\"strong\">would</span> and <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't</span></br></br>  When you want to express the fact that someone was <span class=\"italic\">generally</span> (not for one action) willing to do something in past, you can use <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">would</span></span>. </br> For example: </br><span class=\"italic\"> My neighbor was really nice - she <span class=\"strong\">would</span> always watch over our house when we were away.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't</span> to talk about something (both generally and specifically) that someone was unwilling to do in the past. </br> For example:</br> <span class=\"italic\">I was late for the show because my car <span class=\"strong\"> wouldn't</span></span> start. (specific) </br><span class=\"italic\">My dad <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't</span> help with the dishes, but he would help with the cooking.</span> (general)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">I'll </span>wait for you at a pub called O'Malley's. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">I'll </span>wait for you up until boarding time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">won't</span> wait a second more.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What he <span class=\"strong\">would</span> do is give great pearls of wisdom from time to time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My dad <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't</span> help me with my homework.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "unanticipatedly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not expected", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: One day, unanticipatedly, he said, \u201cSon, in life, you have to know when to roll the dice.\u201d", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when talking about risk management.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pearls of wisdom", "type": "name"}, {"content": "A succinct, insightful saying, piece of advice, or moral precept", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What he would do is give great pearls of wisdom from time to time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "roll the dice", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take a chance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have to know when to roll the dice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "inexperienced", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not having or showing the necessary skills to do something successfully", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Those guys are are so inexperienced!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "careless", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not paying attention to what you are doing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Those guys are careless when they work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stalling", "type": "name"}, {"content": "stop or cause to stop making progress", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was stalling for time while I thought of an answer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research a famous person.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify the times that they took a chance.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify the times when they were successful and when they failed.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about what was advisable in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express whether someone was generally willing to take a chance in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I report to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With the class, brainstorm some famous people.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Select one and do some research on them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Identify all the times this person rolled the dice or took a chance.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Try to identify one time rolling the dice worked and one time that it failed.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Were they generally willing to take a chance? ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "How would you advise them looking back on the situation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Report to your partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs":